.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Vt X509_PUBKEY
structure represents the ASN.1
.Sy SubjectPublicKeyInfo
structure defined in RFC5280 and used in certificates and certificate
requests.
.Pp
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_new_ex
allocates and initializes an
.Vt X509_PUBKEY
structure associated with the given
.Vt OSSL_LIB_CTX
in the
.Fa libctx
parameter.
Any algorithm fetches associated with using the
.Vt X509_PUBKEY
object will use the property query string
.Fa propq .
See
.Xr crypto 7
for further information about algorithm fetching.
.Pp
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_new
is the same as
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_new_ex
except that the default (NULL)
.Vt OSSL_LIB_CTX
and a NULL property query string are used.
.Pp
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_dup
creates a duplicate copy of the
.Vt X509_PUBKEY
object specified by
.Fa a .
.Pp
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_free
frees up
.Vt X509_PUBKEY
structure
.Fa a .
If
.Fa a
is NULL nothing is done.
.Pp
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_set
sets the public key in
.Em *x
to the public key contained in the
.Vt EVP_PKEY
structure
.Fa pkey .
If
.Em *x
is not NULL any existing public key structure will be freed.
.Pp
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_get0
returns the public key contained in
.Fa key .
The returned value is an internal pointer which
.Sy MUST NOT
be freed after use.
.Pp
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_get
is similar to
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_get0
except the reference count on the returned key is incremented so it
.Sy MUST
be freed using
.Xr EVP_PKEY_free 3
after use.
.Pp
.Fn d2i_PUBKEY_ex
decodes an
.Vt EVP_PKEY
structure using
.Sy SubjectPublicKeyInfo
format.
Some public key decoding implementations may use cryptographic
algorithms.
In this case the supplied library context
.Fa libctx
and property query string
.Fa propq
are used.
.Fn d2i_PUBKEY
does the same as
.Fn d2i_PUBKEY_ex
except that the default library context and property query string are
used.
.Pp
.Fn i2d_PUBKEY
encodes an
.Vt EVP_PKEY
structure using
.Sy SubjectPublicKeyInfo
format.
.Pp
.Fn d2i_PUBKEY_bio ,
.Fn d2i_PUBKEY_fp ,
.Fn i2d_PUBKEY_bio
and
.Fn i2d_PUBKEY_fp
are similar to
.Fn d2i_PUBKEY
and
.Fn i2d_PUBKEY
except they decode or encode using a
.Vt BIO
or
.Vt FILE
pointer.
.Pp
.Fn d2i_PUBKEY_ex_bio
and
.Fn d2i_PUBKEY_ex_fp
are similar to
.Fn d2i_PUBKEY_ex
except they decode using a
.Vt BIO
or
.Vt FILE
pointer.
.Pp
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_set0_public_key
sets the public-key encoding of
.Fa pub
to the
.Fa penclen
bytes contained in buffer
.Fa penc .
Any earlier public-key encoding in
.Fa pub
is freed.
.Fa penc
may be NULL to indicate that there is no actual public key data.
Ownership of the
.Fa penc
argument is passed to
.Fa pub .
.Pp
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_set0_param
sets the public-key parameters of
.Fa pub .
The OID associated with the algorithm is set to
.Fa aobj .
The type of the algorithm parameters is set to
.Em type
using the structure
.Fa pval .
If
.Fa penc
is not NULL the encoding of the public key itself is set to the
.Fa penclen
bytes contained in buffer
.Fa penc
and any earlier public-key encoding in
.Fa pub
is freed.
On success ownership of all the supplied arguments is passed to
.Fa pub
so they must not be freed after the call.
.Pp
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_get0_param
retrieves the public key parameters from
.Fa pub ,
.Em *ppkalg
is set to the associated OID and the encoding consists of
.Em *ppklen
bytes at
.Em *pk ,
.Em *pa
is set to the associated AlgorithmIdentifier for the public key.
If the value of any of these parameters is not required it can be set to
NULL. All of the retrieved pointers are internal and must not be freed
after the call.
.Pp
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_eq
compares two
.Vt X509_PUBKEY
values.
.Sh NOTES
The
.Vt X509_PUBKEY
functions can be used to encode and decode public keys in a standard
format.
.Pp
In many cases applications will not call the
.Vt X509_PUBKEY
functions directly: they will instead call wrapper functions such as
.Xr X509_get0_pubkey 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
If the allocation fails,
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_new
and
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_dup
return NULL and set an error code that can be obtained by
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 .
Otherwise they return a pointer to the newly allocated structure.
.Pp
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_free
does not return a value.
.Pp
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_get0 ,
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_get ,
.Fn d2i_PUBKEY_ex ,
.Fn d2i_PUBKEY ,
.Fn d2i_PUBKEY_ex_bio ,
.Fn d2i_PUBKEY_bio ,
.Fn d2i_PUBKEY_ex_fp
and
.Fn d2i_PUBKEY_fp
return a pointer to an
.Vt EVP_PKEY
structure or NULL if an error occurs.
.Pp
.Fn i2d_PUBKEY
returns the number of bytes successfully encoded or a negative value if
an error occurs.
.Pp
.Fn i2d_PUBKEY_fp
and
.Fn i2d_PUBKEY_bio
return 1 if successfully encoded or 0 if an error occurs.
.Pp
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_set0_public_key
does not return a value.
.Pp
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_set ,
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_set0_param
and
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_get0_param
return 1 for success and 0 if an error occurred.
.Pp
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_eq
returns 1 for equal, 0 for different, and < 0 on error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr d2i_X509 3 ,
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr X509_get_pubkey 3 ,
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_new_ex
and
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_eq
functions were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
.Pp
The
.Fn X509_PUBKEY_set0_public_key ,
.Fn d2i_PUBKEY_ex_bio
and
.Fn d2i_PUBKEY_ex_fp
functions were added in OpenSSL 3.2.
